      "sourceTextSha256": "2f95024b93bb4936e46e8598df7294821f01ada9f5111e7c27bb4dbc2aaab73e",
      "text": "Transfer to the airport for your flight to Bogotá. On arrival, transfer to your hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw6lz405-1ivofn2o2t2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:ca36a266c931ce6b",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "91510447dc43d28ad55079c7c480c7a2830ab1d4c0dd1bd5c8f8e12cd9861518",
      "text": "At the scheduled time, set out on a sightseeing tour of Bogotá’s historic center, also known as La Candelaria.\nAt the Gold Museum, you’ll see a collection of around 34,000 pre-Hispanic gold objects and more than 25,000 pre-Columbian artifacts.\nNext, visit the Casa de Moneda and the Botero Collection, which displays work by the internationally renowned Colombian artist Fernando Botero, known for his paintings, drawings and sculptures.\nContinue with a panoramic view of Bolívar Square and its landmarks, including the Cathedral, Casa de Nariño, Liévano Palace and the Palace of Justice.\nEnd the day with an ascent to Monserrate, then return to the hotel.\nPlease note: The Gold Museum is closed on Mondays. The Casa de Moneda and the Botero Collection are closed on Tuesdays.\n\nThe tour is led by an English-speaking guide.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-mw6lz405-1ivofn2o2t2",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      }
    },
